questions.solution:
The mean squared velocity of gas molecules is given by:
\overline{v^2} = \frac{3RT}{M}
Since \overline{v^2} \propto T, the graph between \overline{v^2} and T is a straight line passing through the origin. Hence, graph (1) is correct.

